## Context

[[0390]] screens skip-labelled tickets (the `.ergrc` set, `needs-human`
included) out of raid Phase 1 target selection. The screen runs once, at
selection time. A raid runs for hours: a ticket labelled `needs-human`
after Phase 1 but before its wave's Phase 5 launch is caught nowhere — the
executor spawns and burns the full cycle the label exists to prevent.
Surfaced by verify-gate round 1 on PR #698; recorded there as a log note,
promoted here to a trackable ticket.

## Relevant files

- `skills/raid/SKILL.md` — Phase 5 wave launch; the natural second screen
  point is the per-wave launch loop.

## Actions

1. At each wave's Phase 5 launch, re-read the wave's ticket files and drop
   any that acquired a skip label since Phase 1, routing them to the
   wrap-up briefing exactly as Phase 1 does.

## Test

- Bounded-region guard on the Phase 5 section naming the re-screen, per
  tests/test_needs_human_screen.py's extraction pattern.

## Invariants

- Phase 1 screen unchanged; hunt step 2b unchanged.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Phase 5 launch loop re-screens skip labels per wave
- [ ] Guard test in place, RED-proven against pre-change text
- [ ] `make check-fast` and `make lint` pass